<h4 id="transient-and-recurrent-classes--states">Transient and recurrent classes / states</h4>
<p>We provide the algorithms for computing recurrent classes and
recurrent states, since the ones for transient classes / states are similar (they have been improved in
the package too).</p>
<p>Note that for DTMCs, Corollary <a href="#corollary:comm-recurrence">()</a> guarantees us that recurrent classes
and closed classes are the same. <math><mtext><code>recurrentClasses</code></mtext></math> algorithm similar to
<math><mtext><code>communicatingClasses</code></mtext></math> one, with the difference that parsing the communicating matrix we should
check that the class for the state we are inspecting is closed.</p>
<p>With a similar rationale that the one provided for Algorithm <a href="#alg:commClasses">()</a>,
Algorithm <a href="#alg:recurrentClasses">()</a> and Algorithm <a href="#alg:recurrentStates">()</a> are .</p>
<p>

 <math><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></math> a stochastic matrix
{Do $[C, v] = {<math><mtext><code>commClassesKernel</code></mtext></math>}(P)$}
{Mark all states’ class as not computed :
<math><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0">.</mo><mo lspace="0" rspace="0.1667em">.</mo><mo lspace="0">.</mo><mo>,</mo><munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></math>
}


{$i ∈ \{1, <math><mo lspace="0">.</mo><mo lspace="0" rspace="0.1667em">.</mo><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">.</mo></math>, m\}$}


{$j ∈ \{1, <math><mo lspace="0">.</mo><mo lspace="0" rspace="0.1667em">.</mo><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">.</mo></math>, m\}$}
{$C<sub>ij</sub>$}
{$B := B <math><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">⋃</mo></math> \{j\}$}



{$A := A <math><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">⋃</mo></math> \{B\}$}





{<math><mtext><code>recurrentClasses</code></mtext></math> algorithm}

</p>
<p>

 <math><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></math> a stochastic matrix

